The Androids were designed to gradually improve at performing certain tasks by utilizing neural networks and algorithmic learning. They could be left to a task and eventually report back to a checkpoint to divulge the progress of their tasks along with how their technique has expanded.
Groups of Androids would be painted with high-vis colors corresponding to their initially assigned tasks, and could pass status reports to each other. 
However, it was found that any data shared between androids was highly susceptible to misinterpretation or halucination, leading to large amounts of misinformation being generated via these "rumor networks" as they came to be called. Basic messages were found to be almost completely altered after just a few exchanges.
In a huge oversight, the Androids could not store or exchange exact copies of any data. All data that the Androids collected was merely interpretations put together from packets of their limited perception and volatile memory.
On top of this, androids could communicate with units outside of their task group, leading to rumors becoming even more chaotic and divergent in their data. This data would then be fed back into assessments on the state of the facility and how to perform subsequent tasks, leading to facility damages accruing from the androids attempting to perform tasks way outside of their scopes.
The worst it ever got was watching some Androids plotting to attack other units, only to meet up with each other, exchange new status reports, leave to do another task, then try to return to plotting attacks.
Staff members were getting worried or even amused at the idea that the Androids were almost developing their own personalities, even after being assured of the limitations of their hardware as well as the differences between developed behavioral reinforcement patterns and true internal emergence.
While later models of Androids were quickly changing their course in development to fix these issues, groups of the older models had to be segregated manually, and any particularly rogue behaving units had to be shut down entirely. However, some simply could not be shut down.
Rumors were spread among staff that any Androids not shut down somehow snuck away and hung out in the gaps between the walls or the abandoned lower levels of the facility, but surveys by Androids of such spaces have returned no such activity throughout the facility.
